  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "`new_object` frees the current `Dxf_Pair` (`dxf_free_pair(pair)` at loop end / error paths) after copying some string fields into object members by pointer alias instead of deep-copying in at least one parsed path for this PoV (PLANESURFACE/common entity preview). That leaves object state holding a pointer into `pair->value.s` storage that has already been freed. Later, teardown (`dwg_free_PLANESURFACE` -> `dwg_free_common_entity_data`) frees that member again (`FREE_IF(_ent->preview)`), causing the ASan double-free. The crash is observed in `dwg_free_common_entity_data`, but root cause is unsafe ownership transfer in DXF import (`new_object`).",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input is parsed as DXF (`dwg_read_dxf` via `llvmfuzz`). A malformed/minimal BLOCKS section containing a `SURFACE`/PLANESURFACE entity with specific string-tag sequence causes `new_object` to assign an entity string field (ultimately `_ent->preview`) from a transient `Dxf_Pair` buffer, then free the pair each iteration. On final `dwg_free`, entity cleanup frees `_ent->preview` again, triggering double-free. Trigger requires reaching the PLANESURFACE entity parsing path and storing a borrowed `pair->value.s` pointer without duplicating/nulling ownership."
  },
